\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The dual quadric $\mathsf  {Q}^*$ of a cylinder $\mathcal  {C}$ is defined by the set of all planes tangent to the cylinder. From left to right you can see when the number of planes increases the surface resembles the real one more and more. When the number of planes is infinite, the surface is exactly the dual quadric $\mathsf  {Q}^*$.\relax }}{10}{figu